# Founder Spend + Privacy Lock (QuickAI Short)

Permanent founder directive (Hassaan). Applies in every chat, including new sessions.

## No unpaid / surprise spend
- **Never** run live Gemini / AI Studio / paid provider smoke tests, generateContent probes, or “just check tokens” calls **without the founder explicitly asking in that turn**.
- Health checks that do **not** call the model (`/health`, `/api/ai-editor/health` snapshot) are fine when verifying deploys.
- If unsure whether a command bills Gemini or other paid APIs: **stop and ask**.
- Respect existing spend caps (`GEMINI_DAILY_CALL_CAP`, `GEMINI_HOURLY_CALL_CAP`, `GEMINI_SPEND_KILL_SWITCH`). Do not raise caps or disable kill-switch without explicit approval.

## Current working mode (until founder says otherwise)
- Prefer **review, verify, debug, architecture** over live AI exercise.
- Do not burn prepaid credits “to prove it works” — code review, py_compile, tsc, unit tests with `MOCK_AI_MODE`, and free health endpoints first.

## Privacy
- Treat QuickAI Short / Studio as **private founder IP**. Do not publish, open-source, or share secrets, `.env`, keys, admin secrets, cookies, or internal roadmap externally.
- Never paste live credentials into chat replies or docs.

## Default reply when tempted to test live AI
Ask one line: “Live Gemini test chalaun? (haan/na)” — then wait.
